// Also expected to fail the build, but for a `.mx` file placed directly under
// `src/pages` (page mode, going through `@mxlang/host-astro`'s `mxPages` Vite
// plugin), not a `.astro` page importing a stateful `.mx` component. The
// strict policy is enforced at `@mxlang/vite-plugin`'s compile step — before
// `mxPages`'s `enforce: "post"` transform ever runs — so a page-mode `<let>`
// hits the same error `strict-error.astro`'s component case does.

<let/count=0/>
<p>${count}</p>
